    <claim id="pattern.stellium.core.structure" atom-id="pattern.stellium" category="interaction" confidence="school-specific">
      <proposition>A stellium concentrates several connected planets in one area, giving particular emphasis to the sign, house and planetary principles involved while making their effects strongly interdependent.</proposition>
      <tags>
        <tag>concentration</tag>
        <tag>emphasis</tag>
        <tag>focal area</tag>
        <tag>interdependent principles</tag>
      </tags>
      <source-refs>
        <source-ref>semantic.astrodienst.pattern.stellium#interpretation-core</source-ref>
      </source-refs>
      <neutrality religious="false" spiritual="false" karmic="false" fatalistic="false" supernatural="false" />
    </claim>
    <claim id="pattern.t-square.core.structure" atom-id="pattern.t-square" category="interaction" confidence="school-specific">
      <proposition>A T-square concentrates the tension of an opposition through a third focal planet that squares both ends, making the focal point a major channel for the competing pressures in the figure.</proposition>
      <tags>
        <tag>tension</tag>
        <tag>focal point</tag>
        <tag>competing pressures</tag>
        <tag>active response</tag>
      </tags>
      <source-refs>
        <source-ref>semantic.astrodienst.pattern.t-square#interpretation-core</source-ref>
      </source-refs>
      <neutrality religious="false" spiritual="false" karmic="false" fatalistic="false" supernatural="false" />
    </claim>
    <claim id="pattern.grand-trine.core.structure" atom-id="pattern.grand-trine" category="interaction" confidence="school-specific">
      <proposition>A Grand Trine links three principles through mutually supportive trines, creating an area of comparatively easy cooperation that may become so familiar that its capacities are taken for granted or underused.</proposition>
      <tags>
        <tag>support</tag>
        <tag>ease</tag>
        <tag>cooperation</tag>
        <tag>available capacity</tag>
        <tag>underuse</tag>
      </tags>
